## P37.0 CONSOLIDATE (first — everything else lands in it)                                            status
  · Every built tool moves to domains/<domain>/tools/<category>/<tool>/ : tool.json · engine · ui · css · its .spec ·
    preview · packs/factory/pack.json (its built-in presets, taken OUT of the engine code). build/migrate-tools.mjs
    does the move once, parsing the code (acorn) — no hand edits.
  · ONE loader per domain: domains/<d>/tools/index.js, generated by build/index-tools.mjs from the folders. Adding a
    tool = make its folder (build/new-tool.mjs) + run the indexer. Removing = delete the folder.
  · ONE pack mechanism: pack.json (schemas/pack.schema.json) everywhere. Tool packs live in the tool's packs/; packs
    that span tools (80s, Club, EDM Pads, Sequencer songs) live in domains/<d>/content/bundles/<id>/pack.json, loaded by
    the same generated index. data/preset-packs.js and data/seq-packs.js are retired (their content moves, verbatim).
  · Planned-but-unbuilt tools: domains/<d>/planned/<tool>.spec — never mixed with built tools.
  · Core files of a domain: domains/<d>/core/.
  acceptance: no domains/*/organisms/ folder; every built tool's folder validates (build/validate.mjs); every tool has a
  spec beside its code; the same presets (count and names) appear in every tool as before; full suite green.

## P37.1 DOMAINS FIRST                                                                                  status
  · The first screen asks WHAT YOU ARE MAKING: one card per installed domain (Music Production, Video Editing, Image
    Manipulation, AI Automation, Coding Environment, + any domain a pack adds). Picking one enters that domain's mode;
    you can add tools from any domain at any time (+ Add); "Empty canvas" stays.
  · A shared DATA domain (text · json · number · trigger port kinds) so domains can meet without owning each other's
    types (agents and code both speak text/json; neither owns it).
  · ONE enterprise-grade tool per new domain — the one that adds the capability the domain stands on:
      Video Editing      → Video Clip     load a video, scrub, trim in/out, play locked to the transport, export the
                                          trimmed clip (WebM, with its audio); frames out as an image port.
      Image Manipulation → Image Adjust   load an image, non-destructive exposure · contrast · saturation · temperature
                                          · tint · curves · crop/rotate, before/after, export PNG/JPEG/WebP.
      AI Automation      → AI Step        a prompt template with {inputs}, a provider you choose (Anthropic / OpenAI-
                                          compatible / local endpoint), your key kept on this machine only; text or
                                          JSON out (validated); retries, timeout, cost/latency log; dry-run mode.
      Coding Environment → Code Cell      write JavaScript; it runs in a sandboxed Worker (no page access) with inputs
                                          and outputs as ports, console captured, time limit, stop; run on input or
                                          on the beat.
    Each: spec (contract + acceptance) beside the code · tests · factory pack · plain errors · keyboard + names.
  acceptance: the start screen lists 5 domains; each new tool mounts, does its job headless in tests, saves/restores.

