## P37.4 SEQUENCER 3 — reach inside tools                                                               status
  · A lane can target a PART of a tool, not only the tool: one key (a note or a drum pad), a chord, a specific sound
    (a preset — the lane switches the tool's sound on that step), any parameter (level lanes, already there), a tool
    action (throw, fill, drop). "＋ Lane" opens a picker that lists the tool's parts from its own ports, pads and params.
  · Per-lane length and rate (polymeter: 16 against 12 against 7), per-lane volume, step probability.

## P37.5 NEW INSTRUMENTS FOR CONTRAST, TENSION AND FEELING                                             status
  · CONTRAST ENGINE ("fights the rhythm") — from listening analysis of Make It Bun Dem (drop), Kill Everybody,
    Centipede: per-step SOURCE SWITCHING (each 16th/32nd plays a different sound from a set — complextro), gated
    silences (the stop IS the hit), half-time ↔ double-time flips inside a bar, triplet/dotted cross-rhythms against
    the straight kick (3:4, 5:8), pitch dives and rises on single steps, stutter rolls that accelerate, call-and-
    response between two sources. Technique only — no melody, lyric or sample of any record.
  · ALCHEMY ("using tension to create") — a tension field over time: you draw how tense each moment should be; the
    tool turns it into harmony (consonance → dissonance by interval roughness), rhythm density, filter/brightness and
    pitch rise, and RESOLVES on the release points. Drives other tools through their ports.
  · FEELING ENGINE — music from feelings (love, hate, longing, joy, fear…) through the polyvagal ladder (ventral =
    safe/social, sympathetic = fight/flight, dorsal = shutdown): each feeling maps to tempo, pulse regularity, register,
    beating rate, roughness and IRRATIONAL interval sets (φ, √2, π, e ratios against just ones). Builds on the
    existing Embodiment Lab and Vagal recipe — extends, never duplicates.
  · "Push ERAVOS past its limits": extreme songs (Song Engine "Contrast" genre) that use all three at their limits.

